From f2a7499654dd7e17cf81ae7524c1effb84efe67a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sungsu Ahn <sungsu_ahn@korea.ac.kr>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:44:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 37/51] kv: per-thread coherence instrumentation of Get/Put
 (build 73; no protocol change)

The paper's KV API (rackobj::Get/Put -> SharedMemoryObjectHandle::Get/Put)
is now counted in the same ObjectThreadCoh / CohSnap fields as the object
API: one Get = one read section (checks sampled 1 in N with the shared
per-thread counter; (A) stale at read_seq_start, (B) PAGE_INCOHERENT at
read_seq_end incl. the slot flush, (C) META_OUTDATE, (D) contended waits of
the whole Get; the slot copy of the accepted attempt is excluded from the
check time), one Put = one write section (wstart = entry .. data copy incl.
switch_rw, create/admit with its log op and reclaim, retries,
write_seq_start; wflush = after the copy .. return, bytes = value bytes
flushed). reserved[3..4] KV creates and their ns, reserved[5..6] KV Gets /
Puts. CreateEntry's critical-path reclaim attempts are timed like
SwitchRW's. Same TSC clamp. Fixes the ObjectThreadCoh estimator comment
(ratio estimator). object-test phase 8: constructed KV cases per counter.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
